# Copy to .env and fill in. Required only to RUN the generation engine.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/  (never commit the real .env)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# VOICE — LiveKit, and nothing else.
#
# These three power BOTH the live Voice-agent call (Agent Studio -> a Voice workflow ->
# Preview Workflow -> Start Call) AND the Details tab's voice preview button. There are
# deliberately no Deepgram or ElevenLabs keys here any more: both vendors were removed
# 9/3/2026 and everything voice goes through LiveKit on LiveKit credentials.
# `npm run audit:voice` fails if a direct call to either vendor's API comes back.
#
# Get these from the LiveKit Cloud dashboard -> Settings -> Keys.
# Without them the workflow page says voice calls are not configured, rather than
# falling back to a different-sounding agent.
LIVEKIT_URL=
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
#
# The hosted worker that answers those calls lives in agent/ and is deployed separately
# with `lk agent deploy` — see agent/DEPLOY.md.

# OPTIONAL — PRODUCTION HOSTING (server.ts). Not needed for local `npm run dev`.
# PORT the production server listens on (Render sets this automatically).
PORT=
# "Sign in with Google" gate — set BOTH client id + secret to require login.
# Create an OAuth client at https://console.cloud.google.com (Web application),
# with Authorized redirect URI = <BASE_URL>/auth/callback . Leave blank = no gate.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Who may sign in (defaults to invoca.com if unset).
ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAIN=invoca.com
# Random string that signs the login cookie — generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
SESSION_SECRET=
# Public URL of the deployment, e.g. https://invoca-demo.onrender.com (used to
# build the OAuth redirect). If unset, it's derived from the incoming request.
BASE_URL=

# OPTIONAL — Gumloop agent that builds the 3 HTML leave-behinds (Voice Screenpop,
# SMS Screenpop, Voice Routing Demo) from just the customer URL, in parallel with
# the platform demo. Without these the artifacts stay unseeded (My Reports simply
# won't show the rows). Get your API key at Gumloop → Settings → API / Credentials.
GUMLOOP_API_KEY=
# Your Gumloop workspace/user id (shown in the "Run via API" panel of a flow).
GUMLOOP_USER_ID=
# Pipeline (saved-item) IDs — one per artifact. If a single pipeline outputs all
# three, put the same id in all three (the code de-dupes the run).
GUMLOOP_PIPELINE_VOICE_SCREENPOP=
GUMLOOP_PIPELINE_SMS_SCREENPOP=
GUMLOOP_PIPELINE_VOICE_ROUTING_DEMO=

# Optional: Mapbox PUBLIC token (pk.…) for the ChatGPT ad screen's map.
# The real ChatGPT page uses Mapbox; with this set our map matches it exactly.
# Public tokens are meant to ship in browser code — restrict it by URL in the
# Mapbox dashboard. Without it the map falls back to tinted CARTO tiles.
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# Optional: Google Places API (New) key for REAL business photos, ratings, hours,
# address and phone in the ChatGPT sponsored placement flyout.
# SECRET, server-side only — do NOT add a VITE_ prefix, it must never reach the
# browser. Enable "Places API (New)" in Google Cloud, restrict the key to that
# API, and add it here + in Render. Without it the flyout falls back to the
# prospect og:image, then the brand mark.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# ---- Feedback completion emails (optional) ----------------------------------
# PREFERRED: Gmail API, because Invoca's Workspace blocks app passwords.
# It reuses the GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / SECRET above, so there is no second app to
# register. Get the refresh token by visiting /auth/gmail on the LIVE site as an
# admin and following the one-time consent; the page shows the value once.
# ⚠️ THIS IS THE SHARED SENDER, AND IT IS NOW A FALLBACK RATHER THAN THE ONLY
#    SENDER. "Tell the account exec" notifications go out from the SE who marked
#    the demo — the gmail.send grant rides the ordinary sign-in, so nobody has to
#    connect anything (engine/gmailTokens.ts). This account covers anyone whose
#    session predates that, and it still sends every feedback notice.
GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN=
GMAIL_SENDER=
#
# FALLBACK: SMTP with an app password. Dead on arrival if the Workspace disables
# app passwords ("The setting you are looking for is not available for your
# account"), which is why the Gmail route above exists.
# Sends FROM your own @invoca.com address TO whoever submitted the feedback, when
# you mark their item Complete on /feedback. Leave blank and everything still
# works; the notification is simply skipped and logged.
#
# SMTP_APP_PASSWORD is a Google APP PASSWORD (16 characters), not your account
# password. Create one at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (requires
# 2-Step Verification on the account).
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_APP_PASSWORD=
# Optional overrides. Defaults are Gmail's, which is what Workspace uses.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_FROM_NAME=Invoca Demo Generator

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADVANCED-SETTINGS CONTEXT PROVIDERS (Gong / Google Drive / Slack)
#
# The launch form's "Advanced settings" panel can pull context about a prospect
# from these and feed it into the generation. All three are OFF until the
# matching variable is set, and the panel says which one is missing rather than
# offering a source the server cannot fetch.
#
# ⚠️ AN ASSISTANT'S CONNECTORS ARE NOT THIS SERVER'S CREDENTIALS. A Claude
# session may hold Gong/Slack/Drive connectors authenticated as the person
# chatting; the deployed app cannot reach those. It needs its own.
#
# docs/INTEGRATIONS.md has what to obtain for each, and why the three use three
# different auth models.

# GONG — BUILT (9/10/2026). One SERVICE credential, so setting it works for
# every SE at once, immediately — no per-user step, unlike Drive below.
# Gong → Company Settings → Ecosystem → API (needs a Gong admin). The secret is
# shown once. Restart after setting these; check /api/status shows
# gongConfigured: true. Each SE then clicks "Look up Gong" in Advanced settings
# on the launch form — there is nothing else to turn on. See docs/INTEGRATIONS.md.
GONG_ACCESS_KEY=
GONG_SECRET=

# GOOGLE DRIVE — BUILT (9/10/2026). PER-USER OAuth on the client that already
# powers sign-in, so GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET above are already set if sign-in
# works. What is missing is the drive.readonly scope, which is why this needs
# its own flag: enable the Drive API, add the scope to the consent screen, set
# this to 1, restart. Each SE then clicks "Connect" in Advanced settings on the
# launch form — there is no per-user token to paste here; it is stored on the
# server's own disk (DATA_DIR/drive-tokens/) once an SE connects. See
# docs/INTEGRATIONS.md.
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_ENABLED=1

# SALESFORCE — BUILT (9/23/2026). Powers "tell the account exec" on a demo mark:
# the platform looks up the prospect's Account by WEBSITE DOMAIN and emails its
# Owner. One SERVICE credential (OAuth 2.0 client credentials on a Connected App),
# so one setup covers every SE and nobody consents to anything — the same shape as
# GONG above, and for the same reason: an account owner is company data, not
# something living in an individual's own Drive.
#   ⚠️ The Connected App must have "Enable Client Credentials Flow" ticked AND a
#      run-as user set, or the token endpoint returns
#      "client credentials flow not enabled for this connected app".
#   ⚠️ SALESFORCE_LOGIN_URL is only needed for a sandbox
#      (https://test.salesforce.com) or a My Domain login host; the default is
#      https://login.salesforce.com.
# Unset = the feature degrades honestly: the mark still saves, the panel says
# "Salesforce isn't connected on this server", and nothing is emailed.
#
# TWO WAYS IN. Set EITHER block; the refresh token is checked first.
#
#   A) REFRESH TOKEN — no admin, ~10 minutes. Run `sf org login web`, log into
#      the production org, then read ~/.sfdx/<your-username>.json. It uses
#      Salesforce's own pre-installed `PlatformCLI` connected app, which is a
#      PUBLIC client — so there is NO secret here, and sending one fails the
#      exchange. Every lookup reads as whoever ran that command, and it stops
#      working if that account is deactivated.
SALESFORCE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# SALESFORCE_INSTANCE_URL=https://yourorg.my.salesforce.com   # optional; the
#      token response carries its own and that one wins.
#
#   B) CONNECTED APP — the durable answer. Reads as a dedicated service user and
#      survives any one person leaving.
SALESFORCE_CLIENT_ID=
SALESFORCE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SALESFORCE_LOGIN_URL=https://login.salesforce.com

# SLACK — READING messages, for generation context: a workspace app with
# search:read. ⚠️ This is an APPROVAL, not just a variable: installing a Slack app
# to the workspace needs admin sign-off, and this project already has a declined
# request on record for exactly that reason.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# --- Alerts: where "something is wrong" goes ---------------------------------
# ⚠️ A DIFFERENT THING FROM SLACK_BOT_TOKEN ABOVE, and much smaller. That one READS
# messages and needs an app install; this one only POSTS to one channel and reads
# nothing, so it can come from an incoming-webhook app, Slack's own email-to-channel
# address, or a Workflow Builder webhook — engine/alerts.ts cannot tell them apart.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS A CREDENTIAL. Anyone holding this URL can post to that channel, so it
# belongs in the host's environment (Render → Environment) and never in git. This
# file is the NAME on record, not a place to paste the value.
#
# Unset is a supported state: alerts fall back to email (the admin list in
# engine/admins.ts), and to the log if neither is configured. /api/status reports
# which one is live as `alerts.channel` — a label, never the URL.
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Non-production NEVER sends alerts, it logs them — the same rule as ALLOW_EMAIL, so
# a staging service built by copying production's environment cannot page anybody.
# Set to 1 for a one-off test from staging or a laptop.
# ALLOW_ALERTS=1

# --- Replicate: render pages in a real browser (optional, recommended) --------
# Without this, Replicate serves a FAST copy: a plain server fetch that cannot run the
# page's JavaScript, so lazy images, background video and JS-injected icons are missing
# (measured on ridgeline-roofing.com: 21 data-src images and 62 lazy images stay unloaded).
# With it, Browserless renders the page in a real browser first and the replica is accurate.
#
# Why a hosted service rather than Chromium on this server: Render enforces memory PER
# CONTAINER, so a browser here would count against this service's limit — and a container OOM
# kills the whole platform with no chance to catch it. Off-box, the worst case is a less
# accurate replica. Free tier (1k units/month, no card) covers normal use.
#   https://browserless.io  ->  account dashboard  ->  API token
BROWSERLESS_TOKEN=
# Optional: a different region or a self-hosted Browserless.
# BROWSERLESS_URL=https://production-sfo.browserless.io/content
